    "sourceBlob": "492bf2839550ef32a4a3d0a2497e9db2ed438a13",
    "description": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Your waking world is active.</p><hr /><p>Sound is absorbed in your waking world, covering everything in a shroud of quiet until the start of your next turn. Creatures in your waking world become hidden to imprecise hearing or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Concealed] to precise hearing. A creature in your waking world attempting to use spell or effect with the auditory or sonic trait must succeed at a @Check[flat|dc:4]; on a failure, the spell or effect is disrupted. Anytime a creature in the area is affected by an auditory or sonic effect, they must attempt a @Check[flat|dc:16]. On a success, they are not affected by the auditory or sonic effect, though they still may be affected by other aspects of an ability (for example, a creature hit by a weapon with a thundering rune would not take sonic damage but would still take the normal damage from the weapon).</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Requirements Your waking world is active. Sound is absorbed in your waking world, covering everything in a shroud of quiet until the start of your next turn. Creatures in your waking world become hidden to imprecise hearing or Concealed to precise hearing. A creature in your waking world attempting to use spell or effect with the auditory or sonic trait must succeed at a flat check; on a failure, the spell or effect is disrupted. Anytime a creature in the area is affected by an auditory or sonic effect, they must attempt a flat check. On a success, they are not affected by the auditory or sonic effect, though they still may be affected by other aspects of an ability (for example, a creature hit by a weapon with a thundering rune would not take sonic damage but would still take the normal damage from the weapon).",
