    "rarity": "rare",
    "edition": "legacy",
    "publication": "Pathfinder #184: The Ghouls Hunger",
    "path": "packs/pf2e/feats/archetype/ghoul/breath-of-hungry-death.json",
    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/foundryvtt/pf2e/blob/581c2bf2ca9734f4dd83f034fbcc93f8e4fd96eb/packs/pf2e/feats/archetype/ghoul/breath-of-hungry-death.json",
    "sourceBlob": "6b206fa9be64f306896cfb23154578c2cd14f8c7",
    "description": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per hour</p><hr /><p>You have uncovered occult mysteries that allow you to unleash the devastating hunger of Kabriri upon your foes with a single exhalation, releasing a massive cloud of flesh-eating gas that glows with a sickly green light. You deal @Damage[7d6[acid],7d6[void]|options:area-damage]{7d6 acid and 7d6 void damage} to all creatures within a @Template[cone|distance:30] (@Check[reflex|against:class-spell|basic|options:area-effect] save with a DC equal to your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher). A creature that gets a critical failure on this Reflex save is also @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Paralyzed] for 1 round. A creature that succeeds at this save becomes temporarily immune to Breath of Hungry Death for 24 hours.</p>\n<p>When a creature is killed using Breath of Hungry Death, its body is reduced to a smoldering pile of ash wafting with necrotic fumes. You can use a reaction to immediately inhale these fumes and become satiated or fully satiated as if you had used Consume Flesh.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Frequency Once per hour You have uncovered occult mysteries that allow you to unleash the devastating hunger of Kabriri upon your foes with a single exhalation, releasing a massive cloud of flesh-eating gas that glows with a sickly green light. You deal 7d6 acid and 7d6 void damage to all creatures within a cone area template distance 30 (reflex check save with a DC equal to your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher). A creature that gets a critical failure on this Reflex save is also Paralyzed for 1 round. A creature that succeeds at this save becomes temporarily immune to Breath of Hungry Death for 24 hours. When a creature is killed using Breath of Hungry Death, its body is reduced to a smoldering pile of ash wafting with necrotic fumes. You can use a reaction to immediately inhale these fumes and become satiated or fully satiated as if you had used Consume Flesh.",
