    "sourceBlob": "b6fe3a6e3fa4d7bd2716eb7a008565fded631c97",
    "description": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature Casts a Spell with the illusion or mental trait.</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You must have a non-cantrip innate captivator spell with the same trait.</p><hr /><p>Your charms and illusions are so dominant that you can use them to counteract similar magic cast by others. When a foe casts a spell with the illusion or mental trait and you can see its manifestations, you can use your own innate magic to disrupt it. You lose an innate, non-cantrip spell with the same trait as the triggering spell as if you had cast the spell. You then attempt to counteract the triggering spell.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Trigger A creature Casts a Spell with the illusion or mental trait. Requirements You must have a non-cantrip innate captivator spell with the same trait. Your charms and illusions are so dominant that you can use them to counteract similar magic cast by others. When a foe casts a spell with the illusion or mental trait and you can see its manifestations, you can use your own innate magic to disrupt it. You lose an innate, non-cantrip spell with the same trait as the triggering spell as if you had cast the spell. You then attempt to counteract the triggering spell.",
