    "sourceBlob": "e6754de43bd57389f00e21ebcbe29efa59f01378",
    "description": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> During your last action, you succeeded at a melee Strike that dealt physical damage to a creature that can bleed.</p><hr /><p>After striking the target, you run a brush or finger along your weapon to collect a bit of its blood. For the next minute, you can @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Trace Rune]{Trace a Rune} targeting the creature you drew blood from at a range of 60 feet (even if you're Tracing a Rune as a single action). Using Drawn in Vital Ink against a different creature requires you to wipe off the blood already on your weapon, ending the effect for the previous creature.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Requirements During your last action, you succeeded at a melee Strike that dealt physical damage to a creature that can bleed. After striking the target, you run a brush or finger along your weapon to collect a bit of its blood. For the next minute, you can Trace a Rune targeting the creature you drew blood from at a range of 60 feet (even if you're Tracing a Rune as a single action). Using Drawn in Vital Ink against a different creature requires you to wipe off the blood already on your weapon, ending the effect for the previous creature.",
