    "sourceBlob": "623e6232eab27d75d10c2620f4e0445d891a7078",
    "description": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 60 feet uses a fortune or misfortune effect.</p><hr /><p>As someone tries to twist fate, you consume the interference. The triggering effect is disrupted. If it's a misfortune effect, Eat Fortune gains the fortune trait; if it's a fortune effect, Eat Fortune gains the misfortune trait. This fortune or misfortune applies to the same roll the triggering effect would have, so you couldn't negate a fortune effect with Eat Fortune and then apply a misfortune effect to the same roll.</p>",
