    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/foundryvtt/pf2e/blob/581c2bf2ca9734f4dd83f034fbcc93f8e4fd96eb/packs/pf2e/feats/miscellaneous/deviant/enervating-wail.json",
    "sourceBlob": "26005dd32e80dde3e5327d11061c9de4d1ffdf65",
    "description": "<p>You release a terrible wail that tears at the spirits of all nearby. All living creatures in a @Template[emanation|distance:20] take @Damage[((@actor.level - 2)d6)[void]|options:area-damage] damage with a @Check[fortitude|against:class-spell|basic|options:area-effect] save. The damage is 4d6, plus 1d6 for every level you have beyond 6th.</p><hr /><p><strong>Awakening</strong> Your scream echoes in the mind. You can choose to emit a silent psychic wail instead, which changes the damage type to @Damage[(@actor.level - 2)d6[mental]|options:area-damage], changes the save to a @Check[will|against:class-spell|basic|traits:mental,deviant,magical|overrideTraits|options:area-effect] save, removes the auditory trait, and adds the mental trait.</p><hr /><p><strong>Awakening</strong> Your wail saps your foes' strength. In addition to the normal effects, living creatures in the area are @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Enfeebled]{Enfeebled 1} for 1 round on a success (but not a critical success), enfeebled 1 for 1 minute on a failure, and @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Enfeebled]{Enfeebled 2} for 1 minute on a critical failure.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "You release a terrible wail that tears at the spirits of all nearby. All living creatures in a emanation area template distance 20 take damage void damage with a fortitude check save. The damage is 4d6, plus 1d6 for every level you have beyond 6th. Awakening Your scream echoes in the mind. You can choose to emit a silent psychic wail instead, which changes the damage type to damage mental, changes the save to a will check save, removes the auditory trait, and adds the mental trait. Awakening Your wail saps your foes' strength. In addition to the normal effects, living creatures in the area are Enfeebled 1 for 1 round on a success (but not a critical success), enfeebled 1 for 1 minute on a failure, and Enfeebled 2 for 1 minute on a critical failure.",
