    "sourceBlob": "45f2031c1735ee716609dcd7127842fbf9b9ffae",
    "description": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You have condemned a foe with Harsh Judgment.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>You swing wide, attempting to behead your condemned foe. Make a melee Strike against your condemned foe. If you hit, your condemned foe takes 8d6 extra precision damage with a @Check[fortitude|against:class-spell|basic] save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. If the condemned foe is reduced to 0 Hit Points by the execution and requires a head to live, they die. For creatures with multiple heads, this usually kills the creature only if you sever its last head. The creature then becomes temporarily immune to your Execution for 1 day.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Requirements You have condemned a foe with Harsh Judgment. You swing wide, attempting to behead your condemned foe. Make a melee Strike against your condemned foe. If you hit, your condemned foe takes 8d6 extra precision damage with a fortitude check save against your class DC or spell DC, whichever is higher. If the condemned foe is reduced to 0 Hit Points by the execution and requires a head to live, they die. For creatures with multiple heads, this usually kills the creature only if you sever its last head. The creature then becomes temporarily immune to your Execution for 1 day.",
