    "rarity": "uncommon",
    "edition": "legacy",
    "publication": "Pathfinder Lost Omens Character Guide",
    "path": "packs/pf2e/feats/ancestry/human/level-1/keep-up-appearances.json",
    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/foundryvtt/pf2e/blob/581c2bf2ca9734f4dd83f034fbcc93f8e4fd96eb/packs/pf2e/feats/ancestry/human/level-1/keep-up-appearances.json",
    "sourceBlob": "d564a56b66706d6c1e0fd669b97d796c992bc8e7",
    "description": "<p><strong>Access</strong> Taldan nationality</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You are affected by an emotion effect.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Taldan pride means you never show weakness. Roll a @Check[deception] check and compare the result to any observing creatures' Perception DCs. On a success, that creature believes you were unaffected by the emotion effect.</p>\n<p>A creature tricked in this manner can't benefit from the emotion effect and can't use abilities that require you to be under this emotion effect; for example, if you successfully use this ability to trick a will-o'-wisp into believing you aren't under a fear effect, it can't use its Feed on Fear ability on you.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Access Taldan nationality Trigger You are affected by an emotion effect. Taldan pride means you never show weakness. Roll a deception check check and compare the result to any observing creatures' Perception DCs. On a success, that creature believes you were unaffected by the emotion effect. A creature tricked in this manner can't benefit from the emotion effect and can't use abilities that require you to be under this emotion effect; for example, if you successfully use this ability to trick a will-o'-wisp into believing you aren't under a fear effect, it can't use its Feed on Fear ability on you.",
    "descriptionHash": "b165bc2de423408d6f32023fc0261e59ba3aa3950815e29b5f88bf90739e82a6",
    "classification": "native-active",
    "classificationReason": "Native actionType reaction:null; animation follows this feat's own chat card.",
