    "path": "packs/pf2e/feats/class/necromancer/level-14/ocular-flesh.json",
    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/foundryvtt/pf2e/blob/581c2bf2ca9734f4dd83f034fbcc93f8e4fd96eb/packs/pf2e/feats/class/necromancer/level-14/ocular-flesh.json",
    "sourceBlob": "0c48ec8fe77260a80329eb31f4bfb8d66cc4f528",
    "description": "<p>You create a fleshy eyeball that is the size of a marble. You can take a single action, which has the concentrate trait, to look through any of your eyeballs until the start of your next turn. An eyeball can be manipulated like a marble, such as being rolled or thrown. One can also be affixed to a surface, for example a wall, with 1 minute's work. An eyeball lasts for 24 hours, and you can maintain a total of three eyeballs at any given time. Creating a fourth destroys the oldest eyeball.</p>\n<p>Eyeballs are very small but are easy to spot. A creature actively @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Seek]{Seeking} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Search]{Searching} automatically finds an eyeball. They're also not very sturdy and can be destroyed with an Interact action.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "You create a fleshy eyeball that is the size of a marble. You can take a single action, which has the concentrate trait, to look through any of your eyeballs until the start of your next turn. An eyeball can be manipulated like a marble, such as being rolled or thrown. One can also be affixed to a surface, for example a wall, with 1 minute's work. An eyeball lasts for 24 hours, and you can maintain a total of three eyeballs at any given time. Creating a fourth destroys the oldest eyeball. Eyeballs are very small but are easy to spot. A creature actively Seeking or Searching automatically finds an eyeball. They're also not very sturdy and can be destroyed with an Interact action.",
    "descriptionHash": "244336163a48492c2afb79f762e81d2e400131e0d518d5819667436012b2a878",
