    "sourceBlob": "599f982d4a00cc96fa3418ddd52a6c560b2af8f5",
    "description": "<p>Brastlewark snarecrafters know that sometimes it's more advantageous to magically destroy a snare before it's triggered. Choose a magical snare within 120 feet that you crafted. The snare is automatically destroyed and each creature in a @Template[type:emanation|distance:5] takes @Damage[1d6[force]|options:area-damage] damage per level of the destroyed snare with a basic @Check[reflex|against:class-spell|basic] save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC.</p><hr /><p><strong>Special</strong> If you detonate a broad snare or giant snare, choose one square that snare occupies to be the center of the emanation.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Brastlewark snarecrafters know that sometimes it's more advantageous to magically destroy a snare before it's triggered. Choose a magical snare within 120 feet that you crafted. The snare is automatically destroyed and each creature in a type:emanation area template distance 5 takes damage force damage per level of the destroyed snare with a basic reflex check save against the higher of your class DC or spell DC. Special If you detonate a broad snare or giant snare, choose one square that snare occupies to be the center of the emanation.",
