    "sourceBlob": "8219245ce51b60bd644d561ad83cb262999d8cb0",
    "description": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You're in Sky and Heaven Stance.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>You @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Leap] toward an opponent. At any point in the Leap, you can make a single Strike against a creature within your reach. At 12th level, if you hit with this Strike, instead of finishing your Leap, you can immediately attempt a second Leap from the space where you struck the target of your Strike. You can make a single Strike against a target within your reach during this second Leap as well. At 16th level, you can attempt a third Leap if your second Strike hits, and you can attack a target at any point during this third Leap. All Leaps made during this activity gain a +10‐foot status bonus to the total height or distance of your leap, and no two Strikes can target the same creature.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Requirements You're in Sky and Heaven Stance. You Leap toward an opponent. At any point in the Leap, you can make a single Strike against a creature within your reach. At 12th level, if you hit with this Strike, instead of finishing your Leap, you can immediately attempt a second Leap from the space where you struck the target of your Strike. You can make a single Strike against a target within your reach during this second Leap as well. At 16th level, you can attempt a third Leap if your second Strike hits, and you can attack a target at any point during this third Leap. All Leaps made during this activity gain a +10‐foot status bonus to the total height or distance of your leap, and no two Strikes can target the same creature.",
    "descriptionHash": "c71ea55490884886d5d20e9f8de42ea7aaa3cc91ff67a2a528ef761e112c05f5",
    "classification": "native-active",
