    "rarity": "common",
    "edition": "remaster",
    "publication": "Pathfinder Impossible Magic",
    "path": "packs/pf2e/feats/class/magus/level-6/spell-crash.json",
    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/foundryvtt/pf2e/blob/581c2bf2ca9734f4dd83f034fbcc93f8e4fd96eb/packs/pf2e/feats/class/magus/level-6/spell-crash.json",
    "sourceBlob": "94ea7b28c1c7faf24864858a1c546f3cadacdd05",
    "description": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Your Spellstrike is charged, and you have at least one spell prepared in a spell slot.</p><hr /><p>Instead of blending a spell into an attack, you can funnel the spell's magic into a pure blast that expands out from you. You smash your weapon or fist into the ground and expend a spell prepared in one of your spell slots. The magic of the spell explodes out in your choice of a @Template[type:emanation|distance:20], @Template[type:cone|distance:30], or @Template[type:line|distance:60]. Each creature in the area takes @Damage[1d10[force]|options:area-damage] damage per spell rank of the expended spell, with a basic @Check[reflex|basic|against:spell|options:area-damage] save against your spell DC. If your weapon has the shove trait, you push any creature that fails its save 10 feet; if your weapon has the trip trait, any creature that fails its save falls @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Prone]. Your Spellstrike is no longer charged.</p>\n<p>If the spell you expended could deal a type of damage other than force, you can change the explosion's damage to that type and replace Spell Crash's force trait with the corresponding trait.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Requirements Your Spellstrike is charged, and you have at least one spell prepared in a spell slot. Instead of blending a spell into an attack, you can funnel the spell's magic into a pure blast that expands out from you. You smash your weapon or fist into the ground and expend a spell prepared in one of your spell slots. The magic of the spell explodes out in your choice of a type:emanation area template distance 20, type:cone area template distance 30, or type:line area template distance 60. Each creature in the area takes damage force damage per spell rank of the expended spell, with a basic reflex check save against your spell DC. If your weapon has the shove trait, you push any creature that fails its save 10 feet; if your weapon has the trip trait, any creature that fails its save falls Prone. Your Spellstrike is no longer charged. If the spell you expended could deal a type of damage other than force, you can change the explosion's damage to that type and replace Spell Crash's force trait with the corresponding trait.",
