    "sourceBlob": "f3654a8ba7c6b6c176d2d6387d23a5be27e13b50",
    "description": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You're wielding two melee weapons, each in a different hand, and your Spellstrike is charged.</p><hr /><p>Like knives slicing through magic itself, both your weapons carry your spell, delivering it to separate foes. Make a Spellstrike with a spell that can target at least 2 creatures or that has an area. You can make two melee Strikes instead of one, but each must be made with a different weapon and target a different creature. Increase your multiple attack penalty normally after each Strike rather than increasing it for Spellstrike as a whole. If you're in Arcane Cascade, you can apply twofold tine's extra benefit between the two Strikes.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Requirements You're wielding two melee weapons, each in a different hand, and your Spellstrike is charged. Like knives slicing through magic itself, both your weapons carry your spell, delivering it to separate foes. Make a Spellstrike with a spell that can target at least 2 creatures or that has an area. You can make two melee Strikes instead of one, but each must be made with a different weapon and target a different creature. Increase your multiple attack penalty normally after each Strike rather than increasing it for Spellstrike as a whole. If you're in Arcane Cascade, you can apply twofold tine's extra benefit between the two Strikes.",
