    "path": "packs/pf2e/feats/archetype/medic/treat-condition.json",
    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/foundryvtt/pf2e/blob/581c2bf2ca9734f4dd83f034fbcc93f8e4fd96eb/packs/pf2e/feats/archetype/medic/treat-condition.json",
    "sourceBlob": "04b7368ea3638b487673d465f3d616183a5ebd1c",
    "description": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You are holding healer's tools, or you are wearing them and have a hand free.</p><hr /><p>You treat an adjacent creature in an attempt to reduce the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Clumsy], @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Enfeebled], or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Sickened] condition. If a creature has multiple conditions from this list, choose one. Attempt a counteract check against the condition using your @Check[medicine|options:counteract] modifier as your counteract modifier and the condition's source to determine the DC. You can't treat a condition that came from an artifact or effect above 20th level unless you have Legendary Medic; even if you do, the counteract DC increases by 10. Treating a Condition that is continually applied under certain circumstances (for instance, the enfeebled condition a holy character gains from carrying a weapon with the unholy rune) has no effect as long as the circumstances continue.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> Reduce the condition value by 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> Reduce the condition value by 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Increase the condition value by 1.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Requirements You are holding healer's tools, or you are wearing them and have a hand free. You treat an adjacent creature in an attempt to reduce the Clumsy, Enfeebled, or Sickened condition. If a creature has multiple conditions from this list, choose one. Attempt a counteract check against the condition using your medicine check modifier as your counteract modifier and the condition's source to determine the DC. You can't treat a condition that came from an artifact or effect above 20th level unless you have Legendary Medic; even if you do, the counteract DC increases by 10. Treating a Condition that is continually applied under certain circumstances (for instance, the enfeebled condition a holy character gains from carrying a weapon with the unholy rune) has no effect as long as the circumstances continue. Critical Success Reduce the condition value by 2. Success Reduce the condition value by 1. Critical Failure Increase the condition value by 1.",
    "descriptionHash": "7c7af921040f2db4329b83808e271ef48f00e33a6dd9ab83ba9a32ae06ea7773",
