    "publication": "Pathfinder #180: The Smoking Gun",
    "path": "packs/pf2e/feats/archetype/clockwork-reanimator/unwind-death.json",
    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/foundryvtt/pf2e/blob/581c2bf2ca9734f4dd83f034fbcc93f8e4fd96eb/packs/pf2e/feats/archetype/clockwork-reanimator/unwind-death.json",
    "sourceBlob": "17cad5488da177f3d509a7e769a53ccbfaa2a468",
    "description": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The target's body must be mostly intact.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Combining necromancy with the mysterious temporal powers of clockwork, you wind a creature backward from the moment of its death. Attempt a @Check[crafting|dc:40] check to revive a dead creature that has been dead for no more than 3 rounds. If you succeed, the target returns to life with the effects of @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Raise Dead], except it still has the wounded condition it had before dying, increased by 1 (or wounded 1 if it wasn't wounded before dying). Whether you succeed or fail, the target is then temporarily immune to Unwind Death for 1 day.</p>",
    "plainDescription": "Requirements The target's body must be mostly intact. Combining necromancy with the mysterious temporal powers of clockwork, you wind a creature backward from the moment of its death. Attempt a crafting check check to revive a dead creature that has been dead for no more than 3 rounds. If you succeed, the target returns to life with the effects of Raise Dead, except it still has the wounded condition it had before dying, increased by 1 (or wounded 1 if it wasn't wounded before dying). Whether you succeed or fail, the target is then temporarily immune to Unwind Death for 1 day.",
